From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wenwen Fu <wenwfu@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] pipewire: start from the primary ALSA device event

The system PipeWire service inherits dependencies on sysinit.target and
basic.target, which delay it after the primary ALSA control device is
registered.

Make the unit suitable for QuickBoot activation. The service is wanted by
the controlC0 udev add event and starts after its device unit becomes
active. Keep explicit shutdown ordering because DefaultDependencies=no
removes the normal service shutdown dependencies.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [QuickBoot activation is distro policy]

Signed-off-by: Wenwen Fu <wenwfu@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 src/daemon/systemd/system/pipewire.service.in | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/daemon/systemd/system/pipewire.service.in b/src/daemon/systemd/system/pipewire.service.in
index aeddea3..0127f0b 100644
--- a/src/daemon/systemd/system/pipewire.service.in
+++ b/src/daemon/systemd/system/pipewire.service.in
@@ -1,5 +1,10 @@
 [Unit]
 Description=PipeWire Multimedia Service
+DefaultDependencies=no
+Wants=dev-snd-controlC0.device
+After=dev-snd-controlC0.device
+Conflicts=shutdown.target
+Before=shutdown.target
 
 # We require pipewire.socket to be active before starting the daemon, because
 # while it is possible to use the service without the socket, it is not clear
--
2.43.0
